**The Journey of Tom**

Tom was a young boy who lived in a small village near a big river. Every morning, he helped his mother and father with their work. His father was a fisherman, and his mother took care of the house. Tom had a little sister named Lily. She was only four years old and loved to play with her brother.

One day, Tom's father gave him a task. "Tom, you are now old enough to go to the market by yourself," he said. "Take these fish and sell them. Buy some rice and vegetables for dinner."

Tom was excited but also a little nervous. He had never been to the market alone before. He put the fish in a basket and started his journey. The market was in the next village, and he had to walk through the forest to get there.

As Tom walked, he saw many animals. Birds sang in the trees, and rabbits ran across the path. He also saw a monkey sitting on a branch, eating a banana. Tom smiled and waved at the monkey, but the monkey just looked at him and continued eating.

After some time, Tom reached a small river. There was a wooden bridge, but it looked old and weak. Tom was careful as he crossed it. Suddenly, he heard a noise behind him. He turned around and saw a little dog. The dog was thin and looked hungry.

"Poor dog," Tom said. He took a small piece of fish from his basket and gave it to the dog. The dog wagged its tail and followed Tom.

When Tom arrived at the market, it was very busy. People were selling fruits, vegetables, clothes, and many other things. Tom found a place to sell his fish. He called out, "Fresh fish! Fresh fish!" Soon, people came to buy from him. An old woman bought two fish. A man bought three fish. In a short time, all the fish were sold.

Tom was happy. He took the money and went to buy rice and vegetables. He also bought a small piece of meat for the little dog. The dog ate it quickly and wagged its tail again.

On the way home, Tom felt proud. He had done his job well. When he reached the old bridge, he saw the monkey again. This time, the monkey dropped a banana in front of Tom. Tom laughed and picked it up. "Thank you, monkey!" he said.

When Tom arrived home, his family was waiting for him. "Did you sell all the fish?" his father asked.

"Yes, Father! And I bought rice, vegetables, and even some meat!" Tom replied.

His mother smiled. "You did well, my son. You are growing up."

Lily clapped her hands. "Tom is a hero!" she said.

That night, as they ate dinner, the little dog sat near Tom. He had found a new friend. And Tom had learned an important lesson: being kind and responsible made him happy.

From that day on, Tom went to the market every week. He always remembered to help others, whether it was a hungry dog, a kind monkey, or the people in the market. And each time, he felt stronger and wiser.

The end.

